cedia adapts code from the following sources:

- harness2 (Apache-2.0) — budget ledger identity (R rollouts + P sessions per task) adapted into evals/run.ts. Executor, benchmark, and recursion code were not copied.

- ponytail (MIT) — the idea of its "ladder" (no code, then existing code, the standard library, an installed dependency, one line, and only then the smallest new code, with a test for risky logic), restated in cedia's own words in DEEPSEEK_PROMPT (src/core/providers/catalog.ts). Its text was not copied.

- Ink (MIT, Copyright (c) Vadim Demedes) — patches/ink@8.0.0.patch changes its build: Output keeps its caches across frames and reuses an unchanged row's text, Text memoizes its style transform, squashed text and transformed lines are cached, and on the alternate screen a new frame writer (build/log-screen.js) writes each frame by position, moving shifted rows with a scroll region and writing only the changed cells of a changed row. Each change is marked "cedia:" in the patched files.

Claude Code (no license) — read only for understanding; no code copied.

Earlier versions of this repository (the pi package, removed in stage 0) also adapted code from pstack-claude (MIT), Grok Build (Apache-2.0), Codex (Apache-2.0) and oh-my-pi (MIT). That code is no longer in the tree; see git history.
